                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Bought this game in 28/05/2024. 18 days after my brother's death. I'm not the kind of person to get triggered and I needed a way to process all those emotions. However when I saw that there's local co-op (I played games with my brother) it just left a sour taste in my mouth and I dropped it after 2hrs.\n\nNow 857 days later I've completed my spiritfarer journey.   It really does a good job at replicating the complex emotions felt during the grief. The characters in the game aren't perfect (nor are the people that pass away in our life).\n\nMy only issue with the game lies in the gameplay. It felt too sluggish. I wish the game allowed direct instant travel to islands and slow sailing towards the sea (for turtles, jellyfish, comets,dragons). You can skip time from night to morning, but can't skip time from morning to night. It's like the game forced you into multitasking, even if you would sometimes want to just focus on one singular task.\n\nAnother thing that ruined the pacing for me was finding some spirits too late, only after seeing the credits. It's possible to miss them. Which made me disinterested in seeing their story since my journey is over now.\n\nI still enjoyed this game and would wholeheartedly recommended it to people trying to process death of someone close to them.",
